{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ab897a9eb6409869082abfea1fa24269b5b5fb81db918b2553d5780b74be09b9","digest":{"component_or_area":"Reconcile Bridge inbound link applier","key_entities":["inbound_differ._diff_links_inbound","apply_inbound_records._inbound_update_apply_links","graph/_links.py::add_dependency","rebar_reconciler/impossible_links.py",".bridge_state/impossible_links.json","git_adapter.IMPOSSIBLE_LINKS_FILE","reconcile_helpers._commit_binding_store_snapshot","resolve_hierarchy_link","check_would_create_cycle","managed_refs"],"problem_keywords":["inbound link reconciliation","deterministic failure","permanent retry loop","log noise","bridge convergence","dependency graph validation"],"propositions":["Inbound link ADD operations with deterministic structural failures (closed source, redundant ancestry, cycle) are re-attempted identically every reconcile pass because the applier does not record failed verdicts","The reconciler emits the same 19 impossible link writes every ~5-6 minutes indefinitely, generating ~200+ doomed writes per hour and permanent WARNING noise that masks real faults","Failed link attempts are decided by local graph state (endpoint status, parent chain, dependency set, transitive cycle detection) and never change until that state changes, yet no durable memory preserves the outcome across passes","A durable store keyed on structural digests of the inputs that decided each failure allows the applier to skip re-attempts when the digest matches, self-healing when the structure changes"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787537620852006001,"uuid":"f4660983-b8b4-4556-aba2-58b7e975ef53"}